# Loaded by Vite in EVERY mode, so only a local origin belongs here.
#
# This file had two VITE_API_BASE lines — localhost and the deployed box. dotenv
# keeps the last one, so the deployed origin was winning in development too: the
# dev server was calling production, every local db.json edit and server.mjs
# change appeared to do nothing, and nothing errored. The deployed origin lives in
# `.env.production`, which only `npm run build` loads.
#
# `check-docs` now fails on a second assignment here, and on a remote origin here,
# because the effective value of a file with two is invisible.
#
# No trailing slash: client.ts appends paths that begin with one.
# VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:4000
VITE_API_BASE=http://18.205.228.143:4000
